    "description": "Name of the \"Forward messages\" experiment, shown as a toggle title on the Experiments settings page and in settings search",
    "type": "text",
    "placeholders": {}
  },
  "experimentForwardMessagesDescription": "Adds Forward to the message menu, like Telegram: pick a room, then the message waits above the message box until you send it. The sender's name is left out unless you tap it and choose to show it (your last choice is kept); there you can also hide a caption or pick another room. Forwards name the original sender (MSC4553, unstable); other apps see a \"Forwarded from\" line. Forwards from others show who wrote them. No restart needed.",
  "@experimentForwardMessagesDescription": {
    "description": "Explanation under the \"Forward messages\" experiment toggle on the Experiments settings page (also shown in settings search)",
    "type": "text",
    "placeholders": {}
  },
  "experimentMessageDraftsTitle": "Keep drafts",
